// D1602 — a CLOSURE value delivered at every position under a name a module function also
// carries, then CALLED through it. The prelude's `function v(): i32` is what makes each
// function-scoped cell a shadow; the emitter's call arm resolved the callee by name before
// asking the scope, so `v(8)` lowered to a direct `call` on that function.
//
// The ten module-scope positions are still red, at D1661: the shadow is admitted by `vl
// check` there and the call still lowers as a direct one.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
function v(): i32 { 6 }
// @@VALUE@@
(n: i32) => { print(n) }
// @@TYPE@@
(i32) => void
// @@PROOF@@
v(8)
// @@WANT@@
8
// @@SKIP@@
binding: D1661 - a module-scope binding shadowing the prelude's `v` is check-clean invalid wasm
return_inferred: D1661 - the receiving binding is module-scope
return_annotated: D1661 - the receiving binding is module-scope
struct_field_init: D1661 - the destination binding is module-scope
struct_field_assign: D1661 - the rebind is module-scope
array_element: D1661 - the list binding is module-scope
array_element_assign: D1661 - the rebind is module-scope
array_push: D1661 - the rebind is module-scope
global_init: D1661 - a global named `v` beside the prelude's is the same shadow
global_assign: D1661 - a global named `v` beside the prelude's is the same shadow
two_instances: D1661 - both bindings are module-scope
